DESCRIPTION:Transit maps hold a unique place in both the urban environment
  and the cultural zeitgeist\, often transcending their utilitarian purpose
 s to become symbols of cities and nations alike. Iconic transit maps such 
 as Henry Charles Beck's 1933 map of the London Underground or Vignelli's 1
 972 map of the New York subway have been lauded as cultural touchstones th
 at both were inspired by the past and have influenced the future. \n\nYou 
 Are Here is an exhibition that explores the unique relationship between\n
