SUMMARY:[Stanford Cancer Institute] SCI Breast Cancer and African American
  Conference
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T153000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53064389481626-53064389481627@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Black women in the United States continue to face disproportio
 nately higher rates of breast cancer mortality\, often being diagnosed at 
 younger ages\, at later stages\, and with more aggressive forms of the dis
 ease. In response to these persistent disparities\, the Stanford Cancer In
 stitute (SCI) Office of Community Outreach and Engagement\, proudly hosts 
 the SCI Breast Cancer and African Americans Conference. Now in its 15th ye
 ar\, the conference is dedicated to reducing disparities and improving hea
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://stan.md/43SarMh\nLast synced: 2026-08-
 21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Doubletree by Hilton Hotel Newark - Fremont
URL:https://stan.md/43SarMh
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford BeWell / Stanford Healthy Living] Forest Bathing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T110000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52901302285045-52901302287096@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Studies have demonstrated that spending time in nature can lea
 d to a measurable reduction in stress hormones\, as well as improvements i
 n immunity\, blood pressure\, blood sugar levels\, mood\, and cognition. R
 ooted in ancient Japanese traditions\, forest bathing is a full sensory ex
 perience that invites us to connect deeply with the natural world\, calm o
 ur minds\, and experience a sense of peace and well-being.\n\nJoin this in
 -person class to discover the art of forest bathing and experience the ben
 efit\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://healthyliving.stanford.edu/classes
 /register/class_detail.php?t=1cce34dfd3cbss383d348a508b1be48cc821&ci=12527
 25\nLast synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
URL:https://healthyliving.stanford.edu/classes/register/class_detail.php?t
 =1cce34dfd3cbss383d348a508b1be48cc821&ci=1252725
END:VEVENT
